<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ibn Zaydun</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1003–1071</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ibn Zaydun (1003–1071) was an Arab poet of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cordoba">Córdoba</a>, regarded as one of the greatest poets of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-andalus">al-Andalus</a>. He served the Jahwarid government of Córdoba but was imprisoned and fled, and later became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vizier">vizier</a> to the Abbadid kings of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seville">Seville</a>, al-Mutadid and al-Mutamid. His love poems to the Umayyad princess Wallada bint al-Mustakfi and his literary epistles are classics of Arabic literature.</p></div>
